postgresql-@PGMAJOR@-adaptive-autovacuum (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packages for Debian 12/13 and EL10 (RHEL/Rocky/AlmaLinux 10); upgrade script 1.2.0 -> 1.3.0.
  * autovacuum_naptime is managed: halved per check while overdue relations wait and the worker
    pool is under-filled (floor 5 s), decayed back with the cost pair; worker raises need only an
    overdue queue longer than the pool and are no longer blocked by CPU load alone.
  * Table settings are recommended, never written: table_recommendations carries apply_sql /
    revert_sql per database; a recommendation never loosens an operator-set trigger.
  * autovacuum = off is repaired before the sweep and right after a reload; every table counts
    (min_table_bytes 0), dead-tuple floor 1000; vacuum_activity_detail rates are true deltas;
    latest_global_recommendation adds vacuum_read_mbps / vacuum_write_mbps.

 -- adaptive_autovacuum maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

postgresql-@PGMAJOR@-adaptive-autovacuum (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * One control plane per cluster: install once in the control database (postgres);
    every database is discovered and managed without CREATE EXTENSION elsewhere.
  * Cost-weighted vacuum_activity_rate replaces the MB/s signal; XID velocity without
    allocating XIDs; cluster-first status(), database_status, table_status, actions.
  * Installer: --control-database (default postgres); no upgrade script from 1.1.0,
    the helper re-creates the extension.

 -- adaptive_autovacuum maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

postgresql-@PGMAJOR@-adaptive-autovacuum (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

